# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LedgerLens .gitignore — layer 1 of the privacy model (see docs/SECURITY.md).
# Anything that can hold real financial data or a secret is ignored by TYPE,
# not by name, so a statement dropped anywhere in the tree stays untracked.
# The pre-commit hook (scripts/privacy-guard.mjs) is layer 2 and catches
# `git add -f`; CI re-runs the same guard plus gitleaks as layer 3.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
playwright-report/
test-results/
.vite/

# Runtime data: the SQLite database and the drop-folder for real statements
data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Financial documents and exports, by type
*.pdf
*.eml
*.msg
*.mbox
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.ods
*.ofx
*.qfx
*.qif
*.zip

# ...except the synthetic fixtures, which are generated by a seeded script and
# contain no real person, account, or purchase.
!**/fixtures/synthetic/
!**/fixtures/synthetic/**

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
credentials*.json
token*.json
client_secret*.json

# Personal denylist used by the privacy guard. It lists strings that must never
# be committed (address, card digits, loyalty number), so it must never be
# committed itself.
.privacy-denylist

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.log
.claude/
e2e/test-results/
e2e/playwright-report/
